#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354637 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119780 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e4dd07e-475b-5c89-883b-0e4adcf6a723" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Determinant Using the Linearity of the Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59a4042a-f605-574f-a228-ff4ae6d308e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352358} {:answer/id #uuid "73d447eb-1e81-51dc-b291-5725cee52d82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352581} {:answer/id #uuid "74558c61-b294-5a8c-be71-44c0d3822c23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352586} {:answer/id #uuid "b27eb1ec-b060-5c68-b2a6-225457f0de0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353093} {:answer/id #uuid "b5c62a94-26b3-5bea-ae7b-f2fbef1384ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74558c61-b294-5a8c-be71-44c0d3822c23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352586} :answer-field/id #uuid "607dd21d-aeb7-5920-91bc-f439f202ce2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353991}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "27889ca3-5f85-5eb8-aee5-93c6c3d6c2ad" :question/math-academy-id "q-88298" :question/problem "Given that \n$|\\begin{aligned}a+2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ b+3 & 4 & 2 \\\\ c & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|=5,$\nfind \n$|\\begin{aligned}a+1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ b & 4 & 2 \\\\ c & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|.$" :question/worked-solution "We \"factor out\" the given determinant from the determinant we would like to find:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}a+1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ b & 4 & 2 \\\\ c & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}(a+2)-1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ (b+3)-3 & 4 & 2 \\\\ c+0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNow, using the linearity property of determinants and expanding the second determinant across the $3$rd row, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}(a+2)-1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ (b+3)-3 & 4 & 2 \\\\ c+0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| & ={{|\\begin{aligned}(a+2) & -2 & 2 \\\\ (b+3) & 4 & 2 \\\\ c & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|}_{⏟}}_{5}+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5+1\\cdot (-1)^{3+3}|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =5+(-10) \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
